-- EXPECT-ERROR: cannot be widened
-- R4a — WIDENING IS STILL REFUSED, now by the sweep (2026-08-06).
--
-- This case was already rejected before R4a, but for a reason that no longer
-- applies: `cap_narrow : Cap(IO) -> Cap(a)` made its argument literally the
-- root, so ANY non-root argument failed to unify and widening was refused as a
-- side effect of the argument type.
--
-- R4a loosened that to `Cap(a) -> Cap(b)` so attenuation can chain
-- (accept/t148), which moved monotonicity out of unification and into a
-- post-checking sweep. The guarantee is now weaker IN KIND: unification could
-- not be bypassed, whereas an application site the sweep fails to record is a
-- silently permitted widen.
--
-- So this file changes status rather than behaviour. It used to pass for free;
-- it now passes only if the sweep actually works, which makes it the
-- load-bearing witness for R4 rather than a decorative one. The subsumption
-- direction has been written backwards twice in this codebase and shipped
-- once — this is the file that catches the third time.
mod Widen do
  needs IO

  pfn widen(c : Cap(IO.Console)) : Cap(IO.FileWrite) do
    cap_narrow(c)
  end

  fn main(cap : Cap(IO)) do
    println("console cannot become file-write")
  end
end
